{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvajgDWr5kXnHcsq1gQ2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: don't make the non-buyer survey the deciding step. Hold off on launching, and diagnose why people bought and then refunded.**\n\n**What the data says**\n- If about 10,000 saw the offer, 0.3% is roughly 30 buyers. With 40% refunding, about 18 kept it, so net take-up is around 0.18% against a 3% target. That is more than 15× short, and a modest price cut is unlikely to close a gap that size.\n- The 40% refund rate is the more important signal. It suggests people bought on a misunderstanding or a weak promise, so price probably isn't the main problem.\n- Both numbers are small, so treat them as directional.\n\n**Why the survey is weak**\n- Non-buyers will mostly say \"cheaper\" because it's a free answer. Stated willingness to pay overstates real purchase.\n- Most non-buyers probably don't need premium support, or never really noticed the offer. A survey won't separate those cases.\n- The survey is biased towards people who respond, and it can't measure the behaviour you care about.\n\n**Better, cheaper steps**\n1. Talk to the 30 buyers, especially the roughly 12 who refunded. Ask what they expected, what happened, and why they asked for the refund.\n2. Check the offer's exposure and clarity. Did people see it, and what did the copy promise?\n3. Use the control group to see who actually contacts support. That sizes the real addressable segment and shows who might want this.\n4. If a price signal is still needed, run a small randomised price test, for example £8 against £15. That measures behaviour rather than opinion.\n\n**Decision rule:** if the refunders cite a mismatch and the heavy support users are a small segment, reshape or target the offer to that segment. If neither holds, park it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3447,"cache_read_input_tokens":5010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3447},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25e881e4-aebf-446b-9c6e-8508c44fd030","uuid":"a8b938cf-e690-44dc-877e-dfb4b5eb5681","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:09:28.225Z","request_id":"req_011CfvajfysfPRDRjx1TK9j8"}
